<title>SPAIN: Banco Popular lowers prime rate 50 bp to 8.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Banco Popular lowers prime rate 50 bp to 8.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Popular said on Monday that it was cutting its prime rate by 50 basis points to 8.75 percent, effective today.</p>
<p>In addition, it said it was lowering variable-rate mortgages to 7.25 percent from 7.90 percent.</p>
<p>Customer loan rates were also reduced, to 12.75 percent from 13.75 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
